WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:22.395
"We knew it!" Maggie yelled at Joey. "You slashed those tires, didn't you?"

2
00:00:22.396 --> 00:00:25.287
"It wasn't me!" Joey pointed at Tina.

3
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:29.140
"She probably did it, and now she's trying to blame it on me!"

4
00:00:29.141 --> 00:00:34.182
Tina gasped. "I did not do it!"

5
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:37.018
All the commotion was attracting attention.

6
00:00:37.019 --> 00:00:41.305
"What's going on?" Ashley asked, hurrying over.

7
00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:46.273
"This kid slashed the tires!" Maggie cried, pointing at Joey.

8
00:00:46.274 --> 00:00:51.070
"I already told you dummies that I didn't do it!" Joey yelled.

9
00:00:51.071 --> 00:00:55.468
Maggie glared at him. "Why should we believe you?

10
00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:00.240
We heard you teasing Nathan. So we already know you're a bully!"

11
00:01:00.241 --> 00:01:02.713
More people had arrived by then.

12
00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.687
"Wait," the Belltown cheerleader named Melanie spoke up.

13
00:01:06.688 --> 00:01:10.559
"He's telling the truth. He didn't do it."

14
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.425
"How do you know?" Jill asked.

15
00:01:13.426 --> 00:01:18.511
"Because I saw him hanging out right here by the restrooms," Melanie said.

16
00:01:18.512 --> 00:01:22.470
"I was down here for most of the break because I had a stomachache.

17
00:01:22.471 --> 00:01:24.919
He was here the whole time."

18
00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.756
"Are you sure?" Ashley asked.

19
00:01:27.757 --> 00:01:31.129
"Maybe he sneaked away while you weren't looking."

20
00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:35.317
Melanie laughed. "Are you kidding?

21
00:01:35.318 --> 00:01:39.046
Those Valley High colors are so bright you can't miss them.

22
00:01:39.047 --> 00:01:42.323
I would have noticed if he left even for a second."

23
00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:45.196
"Oh." Ashley shrugged.

24
00:01:45.197 --> 00:01:49.894
"Okay, I guess he couldn't have slashed the tires after all."

25
00:01:49.895 --> 00:01:54.976
Just then Ms. Hernandez arrived. "What's all the yelling over here?"

26
00:01:54.977 --> 00:01:58.895
"Nothing," Jill said. "We were just talking."

27
00:01:58.896 --> 00:02:03.302
Joey and Tina stomped off in opposite directions.

28
00:02:03.303 --> 00:02:12.513
Soon most of the other kids wandered away.

29
00:02:12.514 --> 00:02:15.200
Henry led his friends to a private spot.

30
00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:20.277
"I guess Joey didn't do it," he said. "He has an alibi."

31
00:02:20.278 --> 00:02:23.484
"What's an alibi?" Maggie asked.

32
00:02:23.485 --> 00:02:29.350
"It's when someone can prove that he or she wasn't at the scene of the crime," Henry said.

33
00:02:29.351 --> 00:02:33.984
"Joey's alibi is that Melanie saw him by the restrooms.

34
00:02:33.985 --> 00:02:38.642
That means he couldn't have been down at the bikes slashing tires."

35
00:02:38.643 --> 00:02:45.273
"Okay," Maggie said. "I guess he's not the culprit. But what about Tina?

36
00:02:45.274 --> 00:02:48.307
Melanie didn't say anything about seeing her."

37
00:02:48.308 --> 00:02:53.163
"Yeah. And a few people said she disappeared for a while," Cole added.

38
00:02:53.164 --> 00:02:56.749
"She's still a suspect, I guess," Henry said.

39
00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.410
"But we shouldn't focus only on the Valley High kids.

40
00:03:00.411 --> 00:03:02.624
There are other suspects."

41
00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:08.994
Just then he spotted the stranger in the sunglasses walking along, muttering into a cell phone.

42
00:03:08.995 --> 00:03:12.580
"Like him, for instance," he whispered.

43
00:03:12.581 --> 00:03:15.438
"Did either of you question him earlier?"

44
00:03:15.439 --> 00:03:18.625
"Nope," Maggie said while Cole shook his head.

45
00:03:18.626 --> 00:03:21.657
"Let's talk to him now," Henry said.

46
00:03:21.658 --> 00:03:27.090
They hurried after the man, who was heading toward the bike rack.

47
00:03:27.091 --> 00:03:32.508
On the way they passed Ms. Hernandez talking to William. He looked upset.

48
00:03:32.509 --> 00:03:36.142
"Why can't I leave now?" he whined.

49
00:03:36.143 --> 00:03:39.332
"My bike is ruined, and I want to go home."

50
00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:46.182
Ms. Hernandez sighed. "Please be patient. The new tires will be here soon."

51
00:03:46.183 --> 00:03:50.112
"They probably won't even fit my bike," William argued.

52
00:03:50.113 --> 00:03:52.756
"Anyway this ride is no fun."

53
00:03:52.757 --> 00:03:56.853
"Why does he want to quit the bike ride?" Maggie whispered.

54
00:03:56.854 --> 00:04:00.621
"Maybe he feels guilty because he committed the crime."

55
00:04:00.622 --> 00:04:04.230
"But his tire got slashed too," Cole whispered.

56
00:04:04.231 --> 00:04:06.926
"Why would he ruin his own tire?"

57
00:04:06.927 --> 00:04:11.210
"Maybe he did it so nobody would suspect him," Henry said.

58
00:04:11.211 --> 00:04:14.736
"We can question him after we talk to the mystery man."

59
00:04:14.737 --> 00:04:16.323
They kept going.

60
00:04:16.324 --> 00:04:21.194
The man in the sunglasses stopped near his own bike and finished up his call.

61
00:04:21.195 --> 00:04:24.565
"Hi," Henry said, walking up to the man.

62
00:04:24.566 --> 00:04:29.384
"It looks like your tires didn't get slashed, huh? That's lucky."

63
00:04:29.385 --> 00:04:36.737
The man shrugged. "I suppose so. But only nine tires were damaged."

64
00:04:36.738 --> 00:04:39.321
Henry traded a look with his friends.

65
00:04:39.322 --> 00:04:43.509
How did this man know exactly how many tires had been slashed?

66
00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:45.801
It seemed suspicious.

67
00:04:45.802 --> 00:04:49.549
"How did you hear about this bike ride?" Cole asked.

68
00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.390
"Most of the riders are from the Belltown schools.

69
00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:55.129
I didn't know other people even knew about it."

70
00:04:55.130 --> 00:05:00.407
The man looked away. "News gets around, I guess," he muttered.

71
00:05:00.408 --> 00:05:03.580
Henry could tell he didn't want to answer their questions.

72
00:05:03.581 --> 00:05:05.996
That seemed suspicious too.

73
00:05:05.997 --> 00:05:10.452
Luckily Henry's father worked as a reporter at the local newspaper.

74
00:05:10.453 --> 00:05:13.730
He'd taught Henry a few interviewer's tricks.

75
00:05:13.731 --> 00:05:17.926
One trick was rewording the same question in a different way.

76
00:05:17.927 --> 00:05:22.356
"Did you see a flyer hanging up around town?" he asked.

77
00:05:22.357 --> 00:05:25.287
"I bet that's how you heard about the ride.

78
00:05:25.288 --> 00:05:29.226
Or maybe you have a relative that goes to Belltown High."

79
00:05:29.227 --> 00:05:32.866
"Not exactly." The man looked annoyed.

80
00:05:32.867 --> 00:05:37.393
"Actually I'm a news reporter. I'm here to cover the story for the local paper."

81
00:05:37.394 --> 00:05:40.645
"What?" Maggie exclaimed. "But . . ."

82
00:05:40.646 --> 00:05:44.673
Henry elbowed her in the ribs before she could say anything more.

83
00:05:44.674 --> 00:05:47.718
A second later the stranger hurried off.

84
00:05:47.719 --> 00:05:51.541
Cole looked confused. "What was that all about?

85
00:05:51.542 --> 00:05:54.114
Does that man work with your dad, Henry?"

86
00:05:54.115 --> 00:05:56.291
"No," Henry said.

87
00:05:56.292 --> 00:06:05.539
"I know all the reporters at the paper, and that guy isn't one of them. He's lying!"
